# Environment Variables Template

Copy this file and fill in your actual values.

## Backend Environment Variables (Render.com)

```bash
# Database (Neon.tech)
KODA_DATABASE_URI=postgresql://username:password@hostname.neon.tech/koda?sslmode=require

# Redis (Upstash)
KODA_REDIS_URI=redis://default:password@hostname.upstash.io:port

# File Storage (Cloudflare R2)
KODA_S3_ENDPOINT=https://xxx.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
KODA_S3_ACCESS_KEY=your-r2-access-key
KODA_S3_SECRET_KEY=your-r2-secret-key
KODA_S3_BUCKET=koda-files

# Server Configuration
KODA_HTTP_SERVER_PORT=10000
KODA_PUBLIC_URI=https://koda-backend.onrender.com

# JVM Settings (Free tier optimization)
JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx512m -Xms256m

# Email (Disabled for free tier)
KODA_SMTP_ENABLED=false
KODA_SMTP_HOST=
KODA_SMTP_PORT=
KODA_SMTP_USERNAME=
KODA_SMTP_PASSWORD=
KODA_SMTP_DEFAULT_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com
KODA_SMTP_DEFAULT_REPLY_TO=support@yourdomain.com

# Optional: Authentication
KODA_REGISTRATION_ENABLED=true
KODA_REGISTRATION_DOMAIN_WHITELIST=

# Optional: Features
KODA_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false
```

## Frontend Environment Variables (Vercel)

```bash
# Production
NODE_ENV=production

# Backend URL
KODA_BACKEND_URL=https://koda-backend.onrender.com
```

## Notes

- Never commit this file with real values
- Store sensitive values in platform secret managers
- Use different values for staging/production
- Update `KODA_PUBLIC_URI` after deploying backend
- Update `KODA_BACKEND_URL` in frontend config
